# custom IntelliJ IDEA VM options
#
# Tuned for JDK 17/21. The previous version was written for JDK 8 and
# carried flags that are now deprecated (CMS/ConcMarkSweep, removed in 14),
# removed (-Xverify:none), or ignored (-XX:-UseCounterDecay, -XX:+UseCompressedOops
# on 64-bit). Those also made the IDE print a "Deprecated VM options" banner.
#
# If you must still run a JDK 8 IDE, keep the old flags in a separate
# vmoptions file rather than mixing both generations here.

-Xms2048m
-Xmx2048m

# G1 is the default collector on modern JDKs; these only tune its behaviour.
-XX:MaxTenuringThreshold=2
-XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=240m
-XX:SoftRefLRUPolicyMSPerMB=50

-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
-Dsun.io.useCanonCaches=false
-Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true

-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-OmitStackTraceInFastThrow

-XX:ErrorFile=$USER_HOME/java_error_in_idea_%p.log
-XX:HeapDumpPath=$USER_HOME/java_error_in_idea.hprof